Put your messages below what your are replying to. So, the whole
discussion is ordered in the natural way: from top to bottom. Making it
much more easier to 'jump in' or simply to reread parts of it if needed.

And even more: if you're answering several parts of a single message, you
should splt the answered message and insert your answers below each part
in order to make it clear what is an answer to what.

All of this may seems a bit pointless when dealing with rather short
messages and thread but when dealing with long messages and thread, this
becomes just vital in order to still be able to understand something after
a few days of answers.

